  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{3{e}^{2-3x}}{\\sqrt{3}}<-2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{3{e}^{2-3x}}{\\sqrt{3}} & <-2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -\\frac{3{e}^{2-3x}}{\\sqrt{3}} & <-3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -3{e}^{2-3x} & <-3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -3{e}^{2-3x} & <-9 \\\\ {e}^{2-3x} & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({e}^{2-3x}) & >\\operatorname{ln}\u20613 \\\\ 2-3x & >\\operatorname{ln}\u20613 \\\\ -3x & >\\operatorname{ln}\u20613-2 \\\\ 3x & <2-\\operatorname{ln}\u20613 \\\\ x & <\\frac{1}{3}(2-\\operatorname{ln}\u20613).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
